BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Night in Musical Review
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTSTAMP:20261114T171244Z
UID:2d08ae642cd6ca955353bfb927afc9@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The Chaffee Art Center\, Your Center for Creativity\, invites 
 the community to “A Night in Musical Review with a Cinderella Preview" o
 n Saturday\, November 14th performed by artists from Pride's Young Artists
 \, a local community theater company celebrating their 10th anniversary ye
 ar. Doors open at 6pm. Get your ticket for this fun night out! • Dress u
 p! • Prize for the best outfit • Have fun with our Selfie Staging Area
  • Explore our 1890s Queen Anne Victorian Mansion with a History Hunt 
 • Delicious hors d'oeuvres • Enjoy wine and punch • Entertainment wi
 ll include music from Pride's Young Artists Anniversary season and culmina
 ting in a preview of their upcoming show: Rodgers and Hammerstein's Cinder
 ella. The evening will be filled with fun\, food and celebration of music 
 from a variety of local performers of all ages. Each ticket = 2 compliment
 ary glasses of wine\, selection of hors d'oeuvres and entertainment. Seati
 ng is 1st come\, 1st served. $25 per person\, $45 per couple\, $120 to Res
 erve table of 4. Any remaining tickets will be available at the door the e
 vening of the event for $30 per person. Note: This event's proceeds will g
 o toward our Building Fund.\n\nSources: Vermont.com\, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Rutland Area Art Assoc.\, Chaffee Art Center\, Rutland\, VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/a-night-in
 -musical-review-27-10-2026-16-17-50
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Fall Blacksmithing Workshop
DTSTART:20261114T100000
DTEND:20261114T150000
DTSTAMP:20261114T171244Z
UID:fe4e3f6524edbed64c1b0b1947c33c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wanted to learn how to work with fire and shape 
 metal? In this one-day class for adult beginners\, participants will learn
  how to start and manage a fire\, ensure safe blacksmithing practices\, an
 d develop basic techniques for shaping metal including forming a hook\, tw
 isting\, and drifting. At the end of the class\, you will take home a hook
  or bracelet that you’ve made with your new skills! This is a 6-hour pro
 gram with workshop slots available on October 25 and November 14. The cost
  covers the class fee as well as materials. Attendees should bring a lunch
  and plenty of water. Aprons\, gloves\, and ear and eye protection will be
  provided. If you already own protective equipment you would like to use\,
  you are welcome to bring it to class to wear at the discretion of the ins
 tructor. Please wear natural fibers\, long pants\, and sturdy closed-toed 
 shoes such as boots. This class will involve repetitive motions and physic
 al activity with heavy items such as hammers\, and there will be breaks fo
 r all participants throughout. For accessibility questions\, please contac
 t us at info@lcmm.org or 802-475-2022.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Lake Champlain Maritime Museum\, 4472 Basin Harbor Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/adult-fall
 -blacksmithing-workshop-28-08-2026-14-12-43
END:VEVENT
