BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Non-Fiction Comics Festival 2026
DTSTART:20261114T110000
DTEND:20261114T180000
DTSTAMP:20261114T171244Z
UID:b8db366ba1d1cb5daa7817cf27f698@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The fifth annual Non-Fiction Comics Festival will feature pane
 l discussions\, workshops\, and exhibiting cartoonists creating non-fictio
 n and autobiographical work. …With special events and workshops througho
 ut the entire weekend! From science to politics\, history to health care\,
  cartooning has exploded as a legitimate medium for exploring non-fiction 
 topics and the textures of lived experience. With roots in the Vermont Fol
 klife Center’s Non-Fiction Comics Mini-Fest (2017\, 2018 & 2019) and the
 ir partnership with the University of Vermont\, the Pulp Culture Comic Art
 s Festival and Symposium (2017 & 2018)\, NCFS celebrates the full scope of
  non-fiction cartooning with the Fletcher Free Library in Burlington\, Ver
 mont. 2026’s Special Guests include: Gemma Correll\, Mike Dawson\, Tilli
 e Walden\, Jonathan Todd\, Hazel Newlevant\, Sanika Phawde\, Caitlin McGur
 k\, Daryl Seitchik\, Vivian Li\, Katy Doughty\, Stephanie Stalvey\, and Ca
 mila Kerwin. Visit the festival website at: https://www.nonfictioncomicsfe
 st.org/.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fletcher Free Library\, 235 College St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/the-non-fi
 ction-comics-festival-2026-27-10-2026-12-47-07
END:VEVENT
